          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "He bought 40 rackets altogether, and the total cost was $2520. How many of each did he buy?",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "12 tennis rackets and 28 squash rackets. $84r+54(40-r)=2520$ gives $r=12$.",
      "worked": "Let $r$ be the number of tennis rackets. Then $40-r$ is the number of squash rackets.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}84r+54(40-r)&=2520\\\\84r+2160-54r&=2520\\\\30r+2160&=2520\\\\30r&=360\\\\r&=12\\\\40-r&=28\\end{align*}$$\n\nHe bought 12 tennis rackets and 28 squash rackets.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 52
